  "_README": [
    "Race base attributes and per-class attribute adds for the EQ Legends gear planner.",
    "",
    "PROVENANCE — READ THIS.",
    "eqlwiki.com does NOT publish these numbers. Its Character_Races page lists racials,",
    "starting cities and class options only, and is flagged 'outdated' by its own editors.",
    "There is nothing to scrape. So these values are CLASSIC EVERQUEST values, carried",
    "over on the assumption that EQL reuses them. That assumption is UNVERIFIED.",
    "",
    "One thing here IS verified: every class adds exactly 30 points, so a trio is worth 90",
    "to any race (eqltools.com/attributes, read from the game client). The planner asserts",
    "that invariant on load and will shout if you break it while editing.",
    "",
    "TO FIX: make a character, open your stat window before equipping anything, and compare.",
    "Correct the numbers here and set \"verified\": true — the planner reads this file, so",
    "this is the only place you need to touch. Race base = your naked stats minus the three",
    "class adds.",
    "",
    "EQL has no point allocation at creation, so race + 3 classes fully determines the",
    "starting sheet. Players report a soft ceiling of 150 per attribute (unconfirmed);",
    "the planner marks anything over it rather than clamping."
  ],
